# DTF tier manifest: token-virtual-catalog
#   (artifact-keeper#4808 fixed by #4213; artifact-keeper#4215 fixed by #4217)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Both fixes live in the management API (the
# Packages catalog handlers and the service-account handlers) ahead of any
# storage backend, so the oracle is pure HTTP plus direct reads/writes of the DB.
#
# THE BUG (#4808, fixed by #4213)
# Since #4586 a token scoped to a virtual repository reads the virtual's
# members through it on the format routes and /repositories/{key}/artifacts.
# The Packages catalog was left out: GET /api/v1/packages?repository_key=<V>
# expanded V to its leaf members and intersected them with the token's
# allowed_repo_ids, which name only V, so the page was empty (200, total 0);
# GET /api/v1/packages/{id}?repository_key=<V> and .../{id}/versions applied
# the direct per-repository scope to the owning member and answered 404. The
# detail and versions lookups also ignored repository_key as a constraint: a
# package was returned under any context. The fix resolves the context through
# the same member authorization as the other virtual reads (parent visible,
# each private member granted and read-capable for the token's owner) and
# requires the package to belong to that context.
#
# THE FEATURE (#4215, fixed by #4217)
# A virtual-scoped token can read nothing through its virtual for two silent
# reasons: the account holds no grant on a member, or the scope misses it.
# GET /api/v1/service-accounts/{id}/tokens/{token_id}/scope-analysis (admin)
# names each virtual and each unreachable member with a reason from a closed
# set (no_grant, out_of_token_scope); the token list carries
# unreachable_member_count per token and scope_error (invalid_selector,
# selector_matches_nothing, deleted_pinned_repositories); the selector preview
# parses strictly (an unknown key is a 400) and, given service_account_id,
# reports what that account's token would not reach. The analysis and the
# preview's account must be a service account (else 404), and the token must
# belong to the account in the path (else 404).
#
# THE FIXTURE
#   M1, M2   private maven locals; M1 holds com.dtf:tvc-a (1.0.0, 1.1.0),
#            M2 holds com.dtf:tvc-b. OTHER (not in V) holds com.dtf:tvc-c.
#   V        private maven virtual over M1, M2.
#   SA       service account granted read on V and M1, NOT M2 (until the last
#            case); token TV with read:artifacts and repository_ids [V].
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on 1.11.3:
#     #4213  TV list V -> exactly tvc-a reported under V (tvc-b stays out: no
#            grant on M2); TV detail and versions of tvc-a in V -> 200, versions
#            1.0.0,1.1.0, key V; TV detail of tvc-b in V -> 404. Admin detail
#            and versions of a package under a repository_key that does not hold
#            it (another hosted repo, the virtual, a sibling member) -> 404.
#     #4217  analysis of TV -> exactly [{V, [{M2, no_grant}]}], count 1, no
#            scope_error, token list count 1; admin-only (non-admin and the token
#            itself 403/404) and 404 under another service account, a
#            non-service-account user, or an unknown token id; preview refuses
#            {"match_formatz":...} with 400 "unknown field" and a non-object
#            selector; preview on behalf of SA reports [{V, [{M2, no_grant}]}];
#            preview on behalf of a plain user is 404; a selector tampered in
#            api_tokens to an unknown key reports scope_error=invalid_selector
#            on the token list and the analysis.
#     both   after granting SA read on M2: analysis [] / 0, TV list V shows
#            tvc-a and tvc-b, and TV still lists nothing from M2 directly.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: the unscoped admin lists both members'
#              packages under V and reads tvc-a directly and under V; TV reads
#              nothing outside the virtual context (M1 listing empty, unfiltered
#              listing has no fixture package, detail/versions without context
#              404, GET /repositories/M1 403/404, OTHER empty); the preview of a
#              valid selector matches V alone; the token list shows TV pinned
#              to [V]; a non-admin preview is refused.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~70 back-to-back calls across four principals.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
